  "question": {
    "text": "Two identical capacitors have same capacitance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>. One of them is charged to the potential <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi></math> and other to the potential <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>V</mi></math>. The negative ends of both are connected together. When the positive ends are also joined together, the decrease in energy of the combined system is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Jos3h",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "oDs5n",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "hppih",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "5Lhon",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The common potential after connection would be, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mi>V</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>V</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>V</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Therefore, loss of energy</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>C</mi><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>V</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>C</mi><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>V</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math></p>",
